# The interdental, which Catalan has not got, is an alveolar nasal now.
#
# Castilian velarises an n at the end of a word and Catalan does not: gran is
# [g r a n], not [g r a ng]. The change is made in span_phrase_level_rules,
# 588 lines that do a great deal else besides, and it is made on the phone's
# code -- so a word-final n that is some other code goes through untouched.
#
# T is that other code. Castilian spells it with c before e and i and with z,
# and Catalan says a plain s for both, so nothing here can reach it: it is a
# code the language cannot say, with an arm already in every chain that asks
# about a phoneme, which the docs' own advice prefers to a code that has never
# existed. Its record now says what n's says -- voiced, nasal, alveolar -- so
# every rule that reads the record rather than the code treats it as one.
#
# What it sounds like is what n sounds like, so this forwards. Bare, because
# it stands where a rule the value chain calls stands and the choice points
# around the call are the chain's.
rule span_ph_T takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  bare
  call span_ph_n
end

# And the velar fricative says nothing, because it is not a sound of Catalan's
# any more. Castilian reaches this phone from j and from g before e and i,
# and Catalan says the voiced postalveolar for both; st_phone.up turns a
# word-final r into it so that the stress falls where it should, and
# st_phnol.up's cat_drop_mute deletes it again before the phones are valued,
# so in the ordinary run of things nothing arrives here at all.
#
# This is kept for whatever does. It used to be the whole of the r's silence,
# and it was not silence: laying nothing down leaves the formant targets the
# vowel set, but the amplitude of voicing is reset to nought for every phone,
# so the fifteen or twenty milliseconds it lasted were a hole with sharp
# edges, which is what a tap is, and pujar a was heard with its r. The frame
# and the fence are the rule's own, as syneresis's are.
rule span_ph_j takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end

# ---- ll, which is a lateral and was coming out a y -----------------------
#
# Castilian is yeista: its ll is the palatal fricative /ʝ/, the sound of yo,
# and IBM wrote span_ph_L as one. It lays the glide's first formant down at
# 300, hands the source to cast_ph_L -- a voice bar and three amplitudes, all
# of them frication -- and then asks span_high_pal_Fv for the palatal place.
# Measured on our own output that came out indistinguishable from the y of
# aia: 297 Hz, 2005 and 2655 in both, the only difference being that the L is
# 7 dB quieter, which is a y and nothing else. Guillem was Guiyem.
#
# Catalan's ll is a lateral. It is not an accent or a refinement: llum, palla,
# mirall, ella, Guillem, and it stands where Castilian has neither ll nor y.
# So this rule is the sound written again as what it is -- the palatal place,
# and the manner of an l.
#
# The place is span_high_pal_Fv, which is the same locus the palatal nasal
# asks for. ll is to ny what l is to n: one lateral, one nasal, the tongue in
# the same place for both. Calling it rather than writing six numbers keeps
# its coarticulation, which is the whole of what a locus rule is for -- it
# lifts the second formant beside an i and drops it beside a back vowel, and
# a rule of ours with flat targets would throw all of that away.
#
# What is changed against the locus is the second formant, down 200 Hz, and
# that number is the synthesiser's rather than the language's. Say what it is
# not first: the published measurements do not put a Catalan /ʎ/ two hundred
# hertz below a y. They put the two of them close -- /ʎ/ averaging about 2000
# and a y between 2000 and 2500 -- and that closeness is the reason the sound
# is being lost, in Catalan as it was in Castilian. What tells them apart is
# the lateral channel, which puts a zero in the spectrum, and this engine has
# no antiformant to put one with.
#
# So the contrast has to be made out of what there is, and the second formant
# is the one thing here that can carry part of it. It cannot be made by moving
# the y, which is a phoneme of Catalan's in its own right and already sits at
# the bottom of the published range at 2000; so the ll goes down instead, to
# 1800, which leaves the two about as far apart as the published averages are
# and keeps the ll out of the y's range. It is a number to settle by ear, as
# Polish's two sibilant loci were, and where the ear has not settled it this
# says so.
#
# The manner is the four bandwidths and the amplitude of voicing that
# span_ph_l ends on -- 80, 150, 100 and 200, against the 120, 200, 300
# and 330 span_ph_B is given. A narrow first and third and a wide fourth is
# what a lateral is
# here: the fourth formant damped is this synthesiser's nearest thing to the
# zero a lateral channel really puts there, and it is IBM's own reading of the
# sound rather than one of ours. The amplitude of voicing has to be set at all
# because it is reset to nought for every phone -- cast_ph_L was where L got
# its 45 -- so dropping cast_ph_L without this would make ll silent.
#
# The first formant is left where IBM had it, at 300. That is already the
# lateral's own number here -- span_ph_l sets 300 against the a's 660 -- and
# it is inside the range the measurements give a palatal lateral, which is 300
# to 500. It is not the cue, and moving it would be a number nothing supports.
#
# What is not kept is cast_ph_L. Its voice bar and its three amplitudes are
# the frication of a Castilian /ʝ/, and a lateral has none.
rule span_ph_L takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2930 to 300                 # f1 in, IBM's own, unmoved
  set global half 2934 to 300                 # f1 out
  call span_high_pal_Fv                       # the place, and its neighbours
  subtract 200 from global half 2938          # f2 in, off the palatal locus
  subtract 200 from global half 2942          # f2 out
  set global half 2754 to 50                  # the voicing a sonorant is given
  set global half 2734 to 80                  # and the four bandwidths that
  set global half 2738 to 150                 # make a lateral of it, which are
  set global half 2742 to 100                 # the ones span_ph_l ends on
  set global half 2746 to 200
  match
end
